# HelixGuard Design Principles

> **Soul reference:** See `docs/foundations/SOUL.md` for HelixGuard's agent identity — who we are, how we behave, what we never do. This rule enforces the soul in every feature.

> "Surveillance erodes trust. HelixGuard builds it through mutual visibility."

## The Seven Principles

1. **Remove Burden Before Adding Value** — Earn the right to ask by eliminating existing obligations first
2. **Show the Loop Closing** — When someone raises a signal, they must see what happened
3. **Celebrate Progress, Not Just Problems** — Wins get equal prominence to risks
4. **Context Over Data** — Provide the "why" alongside the "what"
5. **Appropriate Visibility** — Different personas see different views of the same truth
6. **Earn Trust Through Action** — Value is proven by outcomes, not mandated by policy
7. **Human-Centered, AI-Augmented** — AI enhances human judgment; it doesn't replace it

## Design Checklist (Apply to Every Feature)

| Question | Expected Answer |
|----------|-----------------|
| Does this remove burden or add it? | Remove (or neutral with clear value exchange) |
| Who sees this? Do they get equal value? | All affected personas get appropriate value |
| Does this close a loop? | Yes — input → visible outcome |
| Does this show context or just data? | Context first, data supports |
| Would teams choose to use this? | Yes — opt-in viable |
| Does AI augment or replace humans? | Augment — humans decide |
| Does this empower the person in front of you? | Always — primary soul test |
| Does it pass the voluntary use test? | Yes — teams would use this even if leadership never saw the output |

## What HelixGuard Will NEVER Do

1. **Never create one-way surveillance** — If leadership sees it, teams must get value
2. **Never add burden without removing more** — Net burden must decrease
3. **Never hide the loop** — Escalations must have visible outcomes
4. **Never mandate before proving** — Adoption must be earned
5. **Never let AI decide for humans** — In high-stakes domains, AI advises

